                <pb facs="0476" n="438" xml:id="pg438"/>

                <head>143. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>Prime Minister Zoli and Foreign Minister Pella met with President Eisenhower
                    during the NATO Heads of Government Meeting in Paris. According to the
                    memorandum of conversation of the meeting, which took place on December 17, the
                    President spoke of the need for European integration, with the Italians stating
                    that they too supported such a policy. The leaders also discussed the Italian
                    economy and reviewed the events of the NATO meeting. For text of the memorandum
                    of conversation, see volume IV, pages 242–244.</p>
            </div>
